Maybe I'm not the best person to answer this for you, having lost a
Valk to poisoned food not half an hour ago, but there are a few simple
guidelines.

-There are two varieties of "food poisoning." First, there's eating
poisonous food ("Eech! That must have been poisonous!"), which works
like a poison from a killer bee or any other poisonous monster.
Barbarians and orcs don't have to worry about this (or any other bona
fide poisoning). For other classes (like my unfortunate valk), know
that certain corpses are poisonous. For starters, kobolds, killer
bees, and snakes--basically anything that can poison you while alive
is a bad idea. Some, like the kobold that did Silvie in, you just
learn to avoid. In any case, this won't directly kill you, just damage
your hp.
-The other sort, where the game identifies "food poisoning" as the
cause of death, is what gets most players ("Ugh! This meat is tainted!
You feel deathly sick."). This isn't a toxin, but rather a disease
(think salmonella or e.coli). It comes from spoiled food, i.e. corpses
that have been dead too long. To avoid, don't eat anything that you
didn't JUST kill. Plant matter won't give you food poisoning, although
it will rot away. Conversely, reanimated corpses (zombies and mummies)
are always tainted; stay away.
-If you do happen to get food poisoning, the best cure is to apply a
unicorn horn. If you don't have one of those, it qualifies as a major
problem which your god will fix if you #pray to him--that is, if you
can safely pray.
-In summary, this is one area of NetHack where using real life common
sense will usually keep you alive. Would you eat a carcass you just
found lying on the dungeon floor? Would you eat a poisonous creature?
Would you eat something that didn't stay dead the first time?

There's doubtless a lot of stuff I didn't cover, but you'll be able to
find what you need if you search this newsgroup or even read the
earlier messages on this thread. Happy Hacking!

